# eslint-snapshot-rule-tester format: v1


Test: flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker >> invalid >>> docs/rules/flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker.md incorrect 1
Filename: flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker-incorrect-1.mmd

Code:
  1 | flowchart LR
  2 |   A --> B
  3 |   %% C-->D
  4 |   %%
    |   ^~ [1]
  5 |   %% D-->E
  6 |

[1] mermaid.js reads this `%%` as a vertex with the id `%%`, not as a comment.
    Suggestions:
      - Remove the `%%`: mermaid.js then makes no vertex from this line.
        Output:
          1 | flowchart LR
          2 |   A --> B
          3 |   %% C-->D
          4 |   %% D-->E
          5 |
---


Test: flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker >> invalid >>> docs/rules/flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker.md incorrect 2
Filename: flowchart-no-bare-comment-marker-incorrect-2.mmd

Code:
  1 | flowchart LR
  2 |   A[a
  3 | %%
    | ^~ [1]
  4 | b]
  5 |

[1] mermaid.js keeps this `%%` line in the text, not as a comment.
    Suggestions:
      - Remove the line of only `%%`: the text then no longer holds this line.
        Output:
          1 | flowchart LR
          2 |   A[a
          3 | b]
          4 |
---


